cli-about = The yomi language command line tool
cli-version-about = Print the version
cli-run-about = Run a script, stopping at each line of text
cli-run-arg-file = The script file to run (the entry file)
cli-run-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the entry file, and subdirectories are searched too
cli-run-arg-start = The label to start from (a label name or module.label; defaults to the start label of the entry file's module)
cli-run-arg-persistent = The file for persistent data (persistent vars and the stop points already passed); read at startup (created if missing) and written at every stop point and at the end
cli-run-arg-lenient = Loads with the lenient policy: variables whose type changed get their initial values instead of failing (applies to --persistent and :load)
cli-run-arg-watch = Watches the scripts and the text table, and reloads them when they change (cannot be used with --auto)
cli-run-arg-seed = The seed for random (defaults to the time of startup)
cli-run-arg-texts = The text table file for another language (see `yomi texts template`); the text of plain lines, quote lines and choices is replaced by the translations. In the session, `:texts <file|off>` switches it
cli-run-arg-auto = Play automatically: plain lines, quote lines and waits (flow.wait, flow.wait_input) advance without reading input; only choices and input.* stops read a line from standard input. Choices show their stable IDs, and can be answered by number or by `#id`
cli-run-arg-show_ids = Show the stable ID of each choice option (always on with --auto); a choice can be answered by `#id` as well as by number
cli-test-about = Explore the branches of a script (every choice and input is tried) and compare what each path shows with golden files
cli-test-arg-file = The script file to test (the entry file)
cli-test-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the script file. The golden directory defaults to tests/golden under it
cli-test-arg-start = The label to start from (a label name or module.label; defaults to the start label of the entry file's module)
cli-test-arg-seeds = Explore with the random seeds 0 to this number minus 1 (at least 1; defaults to 1, the seed 0 only)
cli-test-arg-max_states = The maximum number of states to examine; the search stops there and says so
cli-test-arg-max_steps = The maximum number of instructions of one run (defaults to the limit of the VM)
cli-test-arg-events = The data of an event to try at event.wait, as NAME=DATA (split at the first `=`; repeat it for more data of the same name; a name with no data is tried with empty data)
cli-test-arg-golden = The directory of golden files (defaults to tests/golden under the search directory)
cli-test-arg-update = Rewrite the golden files of every path (and remove those of paths that no longer exist) instead of comparing
cli-test-arg-require_coverage = Also fail when a stop point was never reached, an option was never chosen, a label was never entered, or the search was cut off
cli-test-arg-json = Print the result as JSON to standard output
cli-debug-about = Run a script a source line at a time, with breakpoints and inspection
cli-debug-arg-file = The script file to debug (the entry file)
cli-debug-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the script file
cli-debug-arg-start = The label to start from (a label name or module.label; defaults to the start label of the entry file's module)
cli-debug-arg-seed = The random seed (a non-negative integer); made from the start time if omitted
cli-debug-arg-texts = The text table file that replaces bodies
cli-repl-about = Start a REPL: evaluate expressions, run statements and declarations, and try script lines (inside `yomi run`, use `:repl` at a stop point)
cli-repl-arg-file = The script file to load (the entry file); without it, the REPL starts in an empty environment
cli-repl-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the script file, and subdirectories are searched too (only meaningful with a script)
cli-repl-arg-seed = The seed for random (defaults to the time of startup)
cli-repl-arg-persistent = The file for persistent data (persistent vars and the stop points already passed); read at startup (a missing file means new data) and never written back
cli-repl-arg-lenient = Loads persistent data with the lenient policy: variables whose type changed get their initial values instead of failing
cli-decls-about = Print the declaration file (JSON) of the built-in registry (the standard packages) to standard output
cli-check-about = Check a script without running it (with --decls, without the host's Rust code)
cli-check-arg-file = The script file to check (the entry file)
cli-check-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the script
cli-check-arg-decls = The declaration file (JSON written by `yomi decls`); defaults to the built-in registry
cli-texts-about = Tools for text tables (translations of the text lines)
cli-texts-check-about = Check a text table against a script (missing translations, unused translations, wrong ${"{\u200Bn}"} numbers)
cli-texts-check-arg-script = The script file (the entry file)
cli-texts-check-arg-table = The text table file
cli-texts-check-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the script
cli-texts-template-about = Print a template text table to standard output, with the original text of every line that has a stable ID
cli-texts-template-arg-script = The script file (the entry file)
cli-texts-template-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the script
cli-texts-template-arg-text_language = The language name of the text, written in the template (the @lang line); not the display language (--lang)
cli-assign-ids-about = Append automatic stable IDs to the lines that have none (plain lines, quote lines, choice options, stop-command lines)
cli-assign-ids-arg-paths = The script files to rewrite (a directory means every .yomi under it)
cli-assign-ids-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the first script
cli-assign-ids-arg-decls = The declaration file (JSON written by `yomi decls`); defaults to the built-in registry
cli-assign-ids-arg-seed = The seed for generating IDs (defaults to the time of startup; give one to get fixed IDs)
cli-assign-ids-arg-check = Exit with code 1 without writing when some line has no ID
cli-assign-ids-arg-dry_run = Print the IDs and positions without writing
cli-fmt-about = Format scripts in the standard form
cli-fmt-arg-paths = The script files to format (a directory means every .yomi under it); `-` reads the standard input
cli-fmt-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the directory of the first script
cli-fmt-arg-check = Do not write; list the files that need formatting and exit with code 1 if there are any
cli-fmt-arg-stdout = Print the formatted result instead of rewriting the file (one script only)
cli-fmt-arg-stdin_path = The path of the file that the standard input stands for (with `-`)
cli-schema-about = Tools for the schema of saves
cli-schema-freeze-about = Write the schema of the current scripts to schema/v<version>.yomi (run it at a release)
cli-schema-freeze-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the current directory
cli-schema-freeze-arg-decls = The declaration file (JSON written by `yomi decls`); defaults to the built-in registry
cli-schema-extract-about = Rebuild the content of a frozen schema from the schema inside a save (and persistent data)
cli-schema-extract-arg-save = The save file
cli-schema-extract-arg-persistent = The persistent data file
cli-schema-extract-arg-out = The file to write (standard output if absent; it must not exist)
cli-migrate-init-about = Make a template of a migrate block (all comment lines) from the latest frozen schema
cli-migrate-init-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the current directory
cli-migrate-init-arg-decls = The declaration file (JSON written by `yomi decls`); defaults to the built-in registry
cli-migrate-init-arg-write = Append the template to migrations.yomi instead of printing it
cli-release-about = Check the scripts strictly and freeze the schema (run it before a release)
cli-release-arg-root = The directory to search for modules (.yomi files); defaults to the current directory
cli-release-arg-decls = The declaration file (JSON written by `yomi decls`); cannot be used with --saves
cli-release-arg-saves = Saves and persistent data (files, or every file under a directory) to check loading of
cli-release-arg-dry_run = Only check; do not write the frozen schema
cli-codes-about = List the codes (diagnostics, runtime errors, load errors, and so on)
cli-codes-arg-json = Print machine-readable JSON (independent of the language)
cli-codes-arg-packages = Also list the error codes of the standard packages and the core commands
version-line = yomi { $version }

# Severity shown in diagnostics
severity-error = error
severity-warning = warning

# yomi run
run-read-error = cannot read { $path }: { $reason }
run-entry-outside-root = the entry file { $path } is not under the module directory { $root }
run-end = (end)
run-wait = (wait { $seconds } seconds: press Enter to continue)
run-wait-input = (wait for input: press Enter to continue)
run-saved = saved to { $path }
run-loaded = loaded from { $path }
run-no-previous = there is no previous stop point
run-missing-path = { $command } needs a file path
run-unknown-command = unknown command: { $command } (available: :save :load :back :vars :texts :repl :reload :quit)
run-unknown-command-lang = unknown command: { $command } (to switch the text table, use :texts <file|off>)
run-texts-on = text table { $path } is now in use
run-texts-off = back to the original text ({ $path })
run-reloaded = [reload] reloaded (stop point found by {$by})
run-reload-kept = [reload] failed, still running the previous scripts
run-reload-failed = [reload] failed, still running the previous scripts: { $reason }
run-reload-position-lost = the stop point cannot be kept in the new scripts
run-reload-not-stopped = the script is not at a stop point
run-reload-unavailable = :reload needs the entry file, which is not known here
run-unknown-input = type a command starting with ':' or press Enter to continue
run-io-error = { $path }: { $reason }
run-load-by-ordinal = the stop point was found by its position (its ID and hash are gone)
run-load-by-label-start = the stop point was not found, so the script restarts from the top of the label
run-load-added-vars = variables added with their default values: { $vars }
run-load-removed-vars = variables dropped because the script no longer has them: { $vars }
run-load-type-changed-vars = variables whose type changed: { $vars }
run-load-type-changed-locals = local variables whose type changed: { $vars }
run-load-ignored-slices = package state dropped because the package is not registered: { $packages }
run-load-defaulted-slices = package state reset to its default because the save has none: { $packages }
run-load-migrated-slices = package state migrated from an older version: { $packages }
run-load-changed-rules = package rules changed since the save (results may differ): { $packages }
run-persistent-read-failed = cannot read the persistent data { $path }: { $reason }
run-persistent-write-failed = cannot write the persistent data { $path }: { $reason }
run-choose-invalid = enter a number from 1 to { $count }
run-choose-unknown-id = no option with the ID #{ $id } in this list (enter a number from 1 to { $count }, or the #ID of an option)
run-auto-unknown-id = (--auto) the answer { $text } is not the ID of any option in the list
run-auto-invalid-answer = (--auto) the answer { $text } is not a choice: enter an option number or its #ID
run-auto-input-ended = (--auto) the input ended before the answer to a choice
run-auto-unknown-event = (--auto) the answer starts with { $text }, which is not one of the events waited for
run-auto-event-empty = (--auto) an empty answer ends a wait only when it has a time limit, and this one has none
run-event-unknown = no event named { $name } is waited for (enter one of: { $names }, then optional data)
run-event-empty = this wait has no time limit: enter one of the events ({ $names }), then optional data
run-event-input-ended = the input ended while waiting for an event that has no time limit

# yomi run: cues of the audio and image packages (one line each)
run-cue-audio-play = [audio] { $channel } = { $name } volume { $volume } (fade { $fade } s)
run-cue-audio-stop = [audio] { $channel } stop (fade { $fade } s)
run-cue-audio-volume = [audio] { $channel } volume { $volume } (fade { $fade } s)
run-cue-audio-se = [audio] se { $name }
run-cue-audio-voice = [audio] voice { $name }
run-cue-audio-se-stop = [audio] se stop
run-cue-audio-voice-stop = [audio] voice stop
run-cue-image-show = [image] show { $slot } = { $name } at ({ $x }, { $y }) (fade { $fade } s)
run-cue-image-move = [image] move { $slot } to ({ $x }, { $y }) ({ $seconds } s)
run-cue-image-hide = [image] hide { $slot } (fade { $fade } s)
run-cue-image-clear = [image] clear (fade { $fade } s)
run-cue-image-layer = [image] layer { $slot } = { $layer }
run-cue-image-scale = [image] scale { $slot } = { $scale } ({ $seconds } s)
run-cue-image-flip = [image] flip { $slot } = { $flip }
run-cue-image-alpha = [image] alpha { $slot } = { $alpha } ({ $seconds } s)
run-cue-screen-fade-out = [screen] fade out to { $color } ({ $seconds } s)
run-cue-screen-fade-in = [screen] fade in ({ $seconds } s)
run-cue-screen-shake = [screen] shake { $strength } ({ $seconds } s)
run-cue-screen-flash = [screen] flash { $color } ({ $seconds } s)

# yomi run: input of the input package
run-input-text = [input] { $prompt } (text, up to { $max_len } characters; Enter for the default: { $default })
run-input-int = [input] { $prompt } (integer from { $min } to { $max }; Enter for the default: { $default })
run-input-confirm = [input] { $prompt } (y/n; Enter for yes)

# yomi test
test-states = States examined: { $n }
test-paths = Paths that reach the end: { $n }
test-truncated = The search stopped at the limit of { $max } states, so it is incomplete
test-no-answers = (no answers)
test-error-path = Error path (seed { $seed }, answers: { $answers })
test-stuck = A stop point cannot be answered: { $stop } (command { $command }; seed { $seed }, answers: { $answers })
test-unreached-stops = Stop points never reached:
test-unchosen-options = Options never chosen:
test-unreached-labels = Labels never entered:
test-golden-none = The golden directory { $dir } does not exist, so nothing was compared (create it and run with --update)
test-golden-written = Golden files in { $dir }: { $written } written, { $removed } removed
test-golden-mismatch = Golden mismatch: { $file }
test-golden-stale = Stale golden (its recorded answers no longer work): { $name }
test-golden-new = New path without a golden file: { $name }
test-golden-unexplored = Golden file of a path that was not explored: { $name }
test-golden-run-failed = Cannot record the golden of the path { $name }: replaying it failed
test-golden-io = Cannot use the golden directory { $dir }: { $reason }

# yomi run: waiting for an event of the event package
run-event-wait = [event] { $names }
run-event-wait-timeout = [event] { $names } (time limit { $seconds } s)
run-input-invalid-int = not an integer: { $text }
run-input-invalid-confirm = answer with y or n: { $text }

# Runtime errors
vm-step_limit_exceeded = the step limit for one run was exceeded
vm-interrupted = the run was interrupted
vm-call_depth_exceeded = calls (call or fn) are nested deeper than the call depth limit
vm-value_too_large = a value exceeded the size limit
vm-memory_limit_exceeded = the variables hold more data in total than the size limit allows
vm-index_out_of_range = the list index { $index } is out of range (the list has { $len } items)
vm-key_not_found = the map has no key { $key }
vm-integer_overflow = integer overflow
vm-non_finite_float = a float operation produced a result that is not a number (NaN or infinity)
vm-float_out_of_range = the float does not fit in an int
vm-division_by_zero = division by zero
vm-not_stopped = the script is not stopped
vm-already_stopped = the script is already stopped
vm-ended = the script has already ended
vm-poisoned = the script cannot continue after an error
vm-bad_input = the input has the wrong type (expected { $expected }, found { $found })
vm-start_label_not_found = the start label '{ $name }' does not exist
vm-command_missing = the command '{ $name }' is not registered
vm-command_failed = { $code }
vm-unknown_variable = the host variable '{ $name }' is not registered
vm-slice_serialize = cannot save the state of the package '{ $name }'
vm-invalid_random_range = the minimum of random ({ $min }) is greater than the maximum ({ $max })
vm-snapshot_mismatch = the snapshot belongs to a different program
vm-persistent_data = cannot read the persistent data: { $reason }
vm-no_choice_available = no option can be chosen (every 'if' is false or every 'once' option is already chosen)
vm-choice_out_of_range = the choice number { $index } is out of range ({ $count } options)
vm-located = { $message } (label { $label }, line { $line })
vm-located-label = { $message } (label { $label })

# Runtime errors of commands (the key is std-error-<code, with . as ->; see src/std_errors.rs)
std-error-input-max_len_not_positive = the max_len of input.text must be at least 1
std-error-input-text_too_long = the input to input.text is longer than max_len
std-error-input-range_reversed = the min of input.integer is greater than its max
std-error-input-default_out_of_range = the default of input.integer is outside the range from min to max
std-error-input-integer_out_of_range = the input to input.integer is outside the range from min to max
std-error-event-no_names = the names of event.wait must have at least one event
std-error-event-empty_name = the event name at index { $index } of event.wait is empty
std-error-event-duplicate_name = the event name { $name } is listed more than once in event.wait
std-error-event-negative_timeout = the timeout of event.wait is negative ({ $timeout })
std-error-event-unknown_event = the host returned the event { $name }, which event.wait was not waiting for
std-error-event-unexpected_timeout = the host returned a timeout for an event.wait that has no time limit
std-error-flow-negative_seconds = the seconds of flow.wait must be 0 or more
std-error-math-pow_negative_exp = the exponent of math.pow must be 0 or more
std-error-math-bounds_reversed = the lower bound of { $command } is greater than its upper bound
std-error-audio-not_finite = the { $arg } of { $command } must be a finite number
std-error-audio-negative = the { $arg } of { $command } must be 0 or more
std-error-audio-out_of_unit_range = the { $arg } of { $command } must be between 0.0 and 1.0
std-error-image-not_finite = the { $arg } of { $command } must be a finite number
std-error-image-negative = the { $arg } of { $command } must be 0 or more
std-error-image-slot_empty = the slot "{ $slot }" of { $command } is empty
std-error-audio-channel_empty = the channel "{ $channel }" of { $command } is not playing
std-error-image-not_positive = the { $arg } of { $command } must be greater than 0
std-error-image-out_of_unit_range = the { $arg } of { $command } must be between 0.0 and 1.0
std-error-screen-not_finite = the { $arg } of { $command } must be a finite number
std-error-screen-negative = the { $arg } of { $command } must be 0 or more
std-error-text-negative = the { $arg } of { $command } must be 0 or more
std-error-text-empty_arg = the { $arg } of { $command } cannot be empty
std-error-text-result_too_large = the result of { $command } is too large (the limit is { $limit } bytes)
std-error-text-slice_range = the range { $start }..{ $end } of text.slice must satisfy 0 <= start <= end <= { $len }
std-error-text-fill_not_grapheme = the fill of { $command } must be exactly one grapheme
std-error-core-state_type_mismatch = the state type of package { $package } does not match
std-error-core-persistent_type_mismatch = the persistent slice type of package { $package } does not match
std-error-core-dep_not_declared = package { $package } does not declare { $dep } in DEPENDS
std-error-core-dep_not_registered = the package { $dep } it depends on is not registered
std-error-core-dep_is_self = a package cannot read itself with dep (use state)
std-error-core-bad_args = the argument types of command { $name } do not match
std-error-core-package_slice_missing = the package state slice is missing
std-error-core-decl_only_function = commands cannot run with a registry made from a declarations file

# Load errors
load-bad_magic = this is not a yomi save file
load-unsupported_version = unsupported save format version { $version }
load-checksum_mismatch = the save file is damaged (checksum mismatch)
load-corrupt = the save file is damaged
load-label_not_found = the saved label '{ $name }' does not exist in this script
load-module_mismatch = the save belongs to module '{ $name }', which the script does not have
load-command_missing = the command '{ $name }' used by the script is not registered
load-package_slice = cannot restore the state of the package '{ $name }' from the save
load-save_from_newer_version = the save is from a newer schema version ({ $saved }) than the script ({ $current })
load-save_version_unsupported = the save's schema version ({ $saved }) is too old (the oldest supported is { $min })
load-schema_mismatch = variable types differ between the save and the script: { $vars }
load-migrate_failed = migrating variables failed: { $vars }
load-stop_args_failed = the arguments of the saved stop point could not be rebuilt

# yomi check / declaration files
check-ok = no problems found
check-summary = check: { $errors } errors, { $warnings } warnings
decl-error-at = { $message } (at { $path })
decl-error-syntax = the declaration file is not valid JSON (line { $line }, column { $col })
decl-error-too_large = the declaration file is too large
decl-error-too_deep = the declaration file is nested too deeply
decl-error-not_decls = this is not a yomi declaration file (the format must be "yomi-decls")
decl-error-unsupported_version = unsupported declaration file version { $version }
decl-error-missing_field = a required item is missing
decl-error-wrong_type = the item has the wrong JSON type
decl-error-invalid_type = invalid type name: { $found }
decl-error-invalid_value = the value is not valid
decl-error-registry = the declarations are not a valid registry: { $reason }
vm-decl_only_registry = a registry made from a declaration file cannot run scripts (it is only for checking)
load-decl_only_registry = a registry made from a declaration file cannot load saves (it is only for checking)

# yomi texts
texts-check-ok = the text table matches the script
texts-check-summary = text table check: { $errors } errors, { $warnings } warnings
text-error-invalid_escape = the translation of { $key } has an escape that cannot be used: { $found }
text-error-invalid_placeholder = the translation of { $key } has an embed that is not ${"{n}"} (n is an integer from 1): { $found }
text-error-missing_tab = the line has no TAB between the key and the translation
text-error-empty_key = the key is empty
text-error-duplicate_key = the key { $key } appears more than once
text-error-unknown_directive = unknown directive: @{ $name } (only @lang is available)
text-issue-missing = no translation for { $key }
text-issue-unused = the translation for { $key } is not used (the script has no such line)
text-issue-bad_number = the translation for { $key } uses ${"{"}{ $number }{"}"} but the original has only { $count } embeds

# Compile diagnostics (the key is diag-<code>)
diag-unexpected_token = unexpected token { $found }
diag-unterminated_string = the string literal is not closed
diag-invalid_escape = invalid escape sequence { $found }
diag-invalid_number = cannot read { $text } as a number
diag-full_width_space = a full-width space appears in code
diag-unknown_name = unknown name '{ $name }'
diag-unknown_command = unknown command '{ $name }'
diag-invalid_command_use = the { $kind } command '{ $name }' cannot be used this way (effect and stop commands are written as '@' statements, or as the whole right-hand side of 'let' or '=' when they return a value; query commands are called in expressions)
diag-assign_to_read_only = '{ $name }' is read-only, so it cannot be assigned to
diag-unknown_label = unknown label '{ $name }'
diag-unknown_type = unknown type '{ $name }'
diag-type_mismatch = type mismatch (expected { $expected }, found { $found })
diag-condition_not_bool = the condition must be bool, but it is { $found }
diag-arg_count = '{ $name }' takes { $expected } argument(s), but { $found } given
diag-unknown_argument = '{ $name }' has no argument named '{ $arg }'
diag-duplicate_argument = the argument '{ $arg }' of '{ $name }' is given twice
diag-missing_argument = the argument '{ $arg }' of '{ $name }' is missing
diag-argument_out_of_order = the named argument '{ $arg }' of '{ $name }' must follow the declared order
diag-positional_after_named = a positional argument of '{ $name }' follows a named argument
diag-required_after_default = the argument '{ $arg }' of '{ $name }' has no default but follows an argument with a default
diag-duplicate_name = the name '{ $name }' is already defined
diag-duplicate_stable_id = the stable ID '{ $id }' is used twice in the same label
diag-invalid_stable_id = the stable ID '{ $id }' is not valid
diag-unbound_sugar = no command is bound to the { $kind } line
diag-unterminated_block = a block is not closed
diag-unexpected_close = a closing { "}" } has no matching opening brace
diag-else_without_if = 'else' without 'if'
diag-statement_outside_label = a statement or text line is outside any label
diag-not_constant = the initial value must be a constant
diag-not_yet_supported = '{ $what }' is not supported yet
diag-unexpected_eol = the line ends too early
diag-too_deep = the expression is nested or chained too deeply (up to { $limit } terms)
diag-block_too_deep = blocks are nested too deeply (up to { $limit } levels)
diag-too_many_registers = a label or fn uses too many registers (up to { $limit })
diag-invalid_operation = '{ $op }' cannot be used with { $type }
diag-declaration_not_allowed = '{ $what }' cannot be declared inside a label
diag-outside_loop = '{ $what }' can only be used inside a loop (while or for)
diag-shadowed_builtin = the variable '{ $name }' has the same name as a built-in function (the built-in function can no longer be used)
diag-import_not_first = 'import' must come before every other declaration
diag-unknown_module = unknown module '{ $name }'
diag-module_not_imported = the module '{ $name }' is not imported
diag-duplicate_module = the module name '{ $name }' is used twice
diag-invalid_module_name = '{ $name }' cannot be used as a module name (it must be an identifier)
diag-package_alias = the package '{ $name }' cannot be given an alias with 'as'
diag-duplicate_import = '{ $name }' is already imported (use 'as' to give it another name)
diag-unused_import = '{ $name }' is imported but never used
diag-unused_variable = '{ $name }' is declared but never read
diag-jump_to_callable_label = '{ $name }' has parameters or a return type, so it cannot be jumped to (use call)
diag-jump_in_returning_label = 'jump' cannot be used inside the label '{ $name }', which has a return type
diag-call_in_expression = 'call' cannot be used inside an expression (write it as a statement, or after 'let' or '=')
diag-call_without_value = '{ $name }' has no return value to receive
diag-missing_return = the label or fn '{ $name }' has a return type, but can reach its end without returning
diag-missing_return_value = this label or fn has a return type ({ $expected }), so 'return' needs a value
diag-unexpected_return_value = this label or fn has no return type, so 'return' cannot take a value
diag-label_falls_through = the label '{ $name }' is never called or jumped to, is not the start label, and does not end with jump, return or end
diag-unterminated_quote = the opening 「 is not closed by 」
diag-unclosed_bracket = the opening '{ $open }' is not closed
diag-text_after_quote = only spaces and a stable ID may follow 」
diag-once_without_id = an option with 'once' needs a stable ID (#id)
diag-empty_choice = 'choice' has no options
diag-schema_name_outside_migrations = '{ $name }' (a versioned schema name) can only be written in the migrations module
diag-invalid_schema_file = the frozen schema file '{ $path }' has a wrong file name or header
diag-schema_hash_mismatch = the content of the frozen schema v{ $version } does not match its recorded hash (do not edit frozen schemas by hand)
diag-duplicate_migrate = there is more than one 'migrate { $version }' block
diag-invalid_migrate_version = 'migrate { $version }' is not valid (the version must be 2 or more)
diag-invalid_min_save_version = 'min_save_version { $version }' is not valid (write it once, first, between 1 and the current version)
diag-unknown_schema_name = '{ $name }' does not exist in the schema of version { $version }
diag-migrate_kind_mismatch = 'rename' cannot move '{ $name }' between a save var and a persistent var
diag-migrate_type_mismatch = the type of '{ $name }' is { $found }, but the schema says { $expected }
diag-duplicate_migrate_target = '{ $name }' is handled twice in this migrate block
diag-migrate_impure_expr = { $what } cannot be used in a conversion expression
diag-missing_frozen_schema = the frozen schema for version { $version } is missing
diag-missing_migrate = the 'migrate { $version }' block is missing (write an empty block if nothing changed)
diag-unhandled_type_change = the type of '{ $name }' changed in version { $version }, but migrate does not handle it
diag-schema_changed_since_freeze = the schema changed after the freeze of version { $version }, but there is no newer migrate
diag-ambiguous_identity = the identity '{ $name }' exists in more than one import: { $candidates } (write module.name to choose)
diag-identity_typo = '{ $name }' is not a declared identity, so this is treated as a plain line
diag-unknown_position = the position '{ $position }' given to seen does not exist in the script
diag-unknown_label_literal = the label '{ $label }' given to visited does not exist in the script
diag-non_exhaustive_match = the match does not cover every value (missing: { $missing })
diag-unreachable_pattern = this arm is never chosen, because earlier arms already cover it
diag-unknown_field = the type '{ $type }' has no field '{ $name }'
diag-unknown_variant = the type '{ $type }' has no variant '{ $name }'
diag-missing_field = the struct literal of '{ $type }' is missing the field '{ $name }'
diag-duplicate_field = the field '{ $name }' is written twice
diag-recursive_type = the type '{ $name }' contains itself (a type cannot be recursive)
diag-cannot_infer_type = the type of this expression cannot be inferred (add a type annotation, e.g. `let xs: list<int> = []`)
diag-unknown_method = the type '{ $type }' has no method '{ $name }'
diag-statement_method_in_expression = '{ $name }' updates a variable, so it is written as a statement, not inside an expression
diag-unsupported_element_type = '{ $method }' cannot be used with the type { $type } (sort_by, min_by, max_by and sort need int, float, str or bool; sum needs int or float)
diag-invalid_map_key = the type { $type } cannot be a map key (a key is an int, str, bool, Identity, or a struct or enum made only of those)
diag-not_allowed_in_fn = '{ $what }' cannot be used inside a fn (a fn only computes values)
diag-assign_in_fn = a fn cannot write to the variable '{ $name }' (it may only read it; assign to its own local variables)
diag-unknown_function = unknown function '{ $name }'
diag-deprecated_command_name = the command { $name } is deprecated; use { $new }
diag-repl_not_allowed = '{ $what }' cannot be used in a REPL input
diag-fn_not_saveable = a value of the function type { $type } cannot be kept where it is saved ({ $what }); function values cannot live across a stop
diag-missing_text_id = this { $kind } line has no stable ID (require_text_ids is on, so every line of text needs a #id)
diag-did-you-mean = { $message } (did you mean: { $suggestions }?)

# yomi assign-ids
assign-ids-no-files = no scripts (.yomi) found
assign-ids-nothing = no IDs to add
assign-ids-plan-line = { $path }:{ $line }:{ $col }: will add #{ $id } ({ $kind }; label { $label })
assign-ids-missing-line = { $path }:{ $line }:{ $col }: no stable ID ({ $kind }; label { $label })
assign-ids-summary = added { $count } stable IDs ({ $files } files)
assign-ids-dry-summary = would add { $count } IDs ({ $files } files; nothing was written)
assign-ids-check-summary = { $count } lines have no stable ID ({ $files } files)
assign-ids-write-error = cannot write { $path }: { $reason }
assign-ids-kind-plain = plain line
assign-ids-kind-quote = quote line
assign-ids-kind-choice = choice option
assign-ids-kind-command = stop command line

# yomi repl / :repl
repl-enter = (entering the REPL on a copy of this stop point: :exit returns here, :help lists the commands)
repl-located-line = { $message } (line { $line })
repl-vars-separator = -- REPL variables --
repl-help-help = :help            list the commands
repl-help-vars = :vars            show the variables (the script's, then the REPL's)
repl-help-defs = :defs            show the fn, struct, enum, import and identity declared in the REPL
repl-help-type = :type <expr>     show the type of an expression (it is not evaluated)
repl-help-apply = :apply           write the changed variables back to the stopped script (only in :repl, at the prompt)
repl-help-reset = :reset           discard the REPL's declarations and changes
repl-help-exit = :exit            leave the REPL (back to the stop point in :repl)
repl-help-quit = :quit            quit everything (exit code 0)
repl-help-cancel = :cancel          discard an input that is still being typed (at the ...> prompt)
repl-help-abort = :abort           cancel the running input while it is stopped at a stop point
repl-unknown-command = unknown command: { $command } (available: { $list })
repl-missing-arg = { $command } needs an argument
repl-not-here = { $command } cannot be used in the REPL (leave with :exit and use it at the stop point of `yomi run`)
repl-not-at-stop = { $command } cannot be used while an input is stopped at a stop point (finish the input, or cancel it with :abort)
repl-abort-not-stopped = :abort can only be used while an input is stopped at a stop point (to discard a half-typed input, use :cancel)
repl-already = already in the REPL
repl-apply-unavailable = :apply can only be used at the prompt of a REPL entered with :repl from `yomi run`
repl-apply-nothing = no variables to apply
repl-apply-skipped = not applied (persistent): { $names }
repl-apply-invalid = cannot apply { $name }: { $reason }
repl-apply-stop-args = cannot rebuild the stop point with the new values: { $message }
repl-apply-reason-type = the value does not fit the type of the variable
repl-apply-reason-too-large = the value exceeds the size limit
repl-apply-reason-memory = the variables would hold more data in total than the size limit allows
repl-apply-reason-not-savable = the value cannot be saved (nested too deeply, or not a finite float)
cli-mcp-about = Run the MCP server on standard input and output (tools: check, format, reserved_words, diagnostic_codes, spec, run, test). The display language comes from YOMI_CLI_LANG, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES and LANG (--lang has no effect)
mcp-instructions = Tools for the yomi scripting language: check a script (check), list the reserved words (reserved_words) and the diagnostic codes (diagnostic_codes), read the specification and the guide (spec), run a script in a sandbox (run), and explore its branches (test).
mcp-error-path-or-source = Give exactly one of `path` and `source`
mcp-error-collect = Cannot read the script: { $reason }
mcp-error-too-large = The scripts and the input are too large (the limit is { $limit } bytes)
mcp-error-module-name = The module name "{ $name }" is not usable (ASCII letters, digits and `_`, separated by `::`)
mcp-error-no-entry = The entry module is missing (the module named `main`)
mcp-error-duplicate-module = The module "{ $name }" is given twice
mcp-error-unknown-part = Unknown document "{ $part }" (known: { $known })
mcp-error-spawn = Cannot start the sandbox: { $reason }
mcp-error-decls = Cannot use the declaration file: { $reason }
mcp-error-event-name = The event name "{ $name }" is not usable (it must not be empty or contain `=`)
mcp-error-seeds = `seeds` must be at least 1
mcp-error-max-states = `max_states` must be between 1 and { $limit }
mcp-tool-check = Check a yomi script without running it and return the diagnostics (errors and warnings)
mcp-tool-check-param-source = Source text of the entry module (named `main`); give this or `path`
mcp-tool-check-param-modules = Other modules that the entry module imports (with `source`)
mcp-tool-check-param-path = Path of the entry script file on this machine; give this or `source`
mcp-tool-check-param-root = Directory to search for modules (with `path`); defaults to the directory of the script
mcp-tool-check-param-decls = Path of a declaration file (the JSON written by `yomi decls`) on this machine; defaults to the built-in registry
mcp-tool-format = Format a yomi script in the standard form and return the result (nothing is written)
mcp-tool-format-param-source = Source text of the entry module (named `main`); give this or `path`
mcp-tool-format-param-modules = Other modules that the entry module imports (with `source`)
mcp-tool-format-param-path = Path of the entry script file on this machine; give this or `source`
mcp-tool-format-param-root = Directory to search for modules (with `path`); defaults to the directory of the script
mcp-tool-reserved_words = List the reserved words of the yomi language and the words that have a meaning only in a fixed position
mcp-tool-diagnostic_codes = List the diagnostic and error codes of yomi with their severity, arguments and messages
mcp-tool-diagnostic_codes-param-packages = Also list the error codes of the standard packages and the core commands (default false)
mcp-tool-spec = Read the language specification and the guide (Japanese Markdown); without `part` it lists the documents
mcp-tool-spec-param-part = Document id such as `language/01-lexical` or `guide/01-getting-started`; omit to list the documents
mcp-tool-run = Run a yomi script in a sandbox (a child process with time, output and memory limits) in auto-play mode
mcp-tool-run-param-source = Source text of the entry module (named `main`)
mcp-tool-run-param-modules = Other modules that the entry module imports
mcp-tool-run-param-input = Lines for standard input: answers to choices and input.* stops (one per line)
mcp-tool-run-param-seed = Seed for random (the run is deterministic with a seed)
mcp-tool-run-param-start = Label to start from (a label name or module.label; defaults to `start` of `main`)
mcp-tool-test = Explore the branches of a yomi script in a sandbox and report the error paths, the stops that cannot be answered and what was not reached
mcp-tool-test-param-source = Source text of the entry module (named `main`)
mcp-tool-test-param-modules = Other modules that the entry module imports
mcp-tool-test-param-start = Label to start from (a label name or module.label; defaults to `start` of `main`)
mcp-tool-test-param-seeds = Number of random seeds to explore, `0` to `seeds - 1` (default 1; at least 1)
mcp-tool-test-param-max_states = Upper bound of the number of states to visit (default 10000, at most 100000)
mcp-tool-test-param-events = Data of events to try at `event.wait`: event name to a list of data (each is tried); a name without data is tried with empty data
mcp-tool-test-param-max_steps = Upper bound of the number of instructions of one run (defaults to the VM default)
cli-lsp-about = Run the language server (LSP) on standard input and output, for editors: diagnostics, completion, go to definition, references and hover. The display language comes from YOMI_CLI_LANG, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES and LANG
cli-lsp-arg-decls = The declaration file (JSON written by `yomi decls`) for the registry of the host; defaults to the built-in registry

# yomi fmt
fmt-nothing = no files need formatting
fmt-summary = formatted { $count } files
fmt-check-summary = { $count } files need formatting
fmt-write-error = cannot write { $path }: { $reason }
fmt-unverified = the formatted script would not mean the same as the original, so it was not written
fmt-stdout-one = --stdout takes exactly one script
fmt-stdin-needs-path = `-` needs --stdin-path
fmt-stdin-outside-root = { $path } is not under the directory searched for modules
fmt-schema-skipped = { $path }: files under schema/ are not formatted

# yomi schema / migrate-init
schema-freeze-latest = { $path } is up to date
schema-freeze-changed = the schema changed after it was frozen: add a migrate block and raise the version
schema-write-error = cannot write { $path }: { $reason }
schema-read-error = cannot read { $path }: { $reason }
schema-extract-versions-differ = the save has schema version { $save } but the persistent data has { $persistent }
schema-extract-nothing = no save was given
schema-extract-exists = { $path } already exists
migrate-init-no-frozen = no frozen schema (schema/vN.yomi) found; run `yomi schema freeze` first
migrate-init-exists = migrate { $version } already exists
migrate-init-nothing = the variables did not change since the latest frozen schema

# yomi release
release-ok = ready for release
release-dry-ok = checks passed (the frozen schema was not written)
release-loads-ok = { $count } saves and persistent data loaded
release-not-a-save = not a save or persistent data (the magic is neither YOMS nor YOMP)
release-no-label = no label to start from

debug-unknown-command = unknown command: { $command } (available: step next finish continue break delete breaks bt frame up down vars print list quit)
debug-bad-number = { $text } is not a number
debug-break-usage = usage: break [module:]line
debug-break-set = breakpoint { $number } at { $module }:{ $line }
debug-break-moved = breakpoint { $number } at { $module }:{ $line } (line { $requested } has no code, so it moved)
debug-break-none = there is no line to run at { $module }:{ $requested } or after it
debug-no-module = there is no module named { $text }
debug-delete-unknown = there is no breakpoint numbered { $text }
debug-breaks-none = no breakpoints
debug-frame-range = there is no frame { $frame } (0 to { $max })
debug-frame-top = already at the outermost frame
debug-frame-bottom = already at the innermost frame
debug-print-usage = print needs a variable name
debug-var-unknown = there is no variable named { $text }
debug-no-source = the source of { $text } is not available

cli-dap-about = Run a Debug Adapter Protocol server over standard input and output
dap-running = the script is running; only pause and disconnect are accepted
dap-not-stopped = the script is not stopped
dap-unknown-request = unsupported request: { $command }
dap-launch-needs-program = launch needs the "program" argument
dap-launch-failed = the script could not be launched (see standard error)
dap-unsupported-condition = conditions, hit counts and log messages are not supported
dap-not-a-script = this file is not one of the scripts
dap-no-line = there is no line to run at or after this line
dap-answer-first = answer the stop point in the Debug Console first
dap-stop-point = waiting for an answer at a stop point
